\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces The running result of different SNE algorithms in \cite  {Kobak_2020}, with (A) being the light-tail t-SNE, (B) the normal t-SNE and (C) the heavy-tailed t-SNE. Heavy tailed variants are producing tighter and finer clusters, while the light-tail version produces results similar to the original SNE. ($t$-distribution will converge to Gaussian if $\alpha \to \infty $.)}}{12}{figure.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
